# Optional overrides for running the engine from source (`make backend-dev`).
#
# The desktop app needs none of this: it starts its own engine and passes the
# database path and data directory itself. When you run the backend by hand,
# the engine reads `.env` from its working directory, so copy this file to
# src/backend/.env and uncomment what you need. Every value has a default.
# Full reference: docs/configuration.md

# ---- App ----
# JWT signing key (openssl rand -hex 32). The desktop app generates its own per install.
# POLARIS_SECRET_KEY=change-me-random-64-chars
# Encryption of stored secrets. Leave unset to derive a key from the secret key;
# never leave a placeholder here, it is not a valid Fernet key.
# (python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet;print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())")
# POLARIS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# Extra origins allowed to call the engine from a browser page (never "*").
# Not needed for `make frontend-dev`, which proxies /api same-origin.
# POLARIS_CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173
# Extra Host names the engine accepts besides 127.0.0.1 / localhost / [::1].
# POLARIS_ALLOWED_HOSTS=

# ---- Storage ----
# SQLite database (the only supported database) and the directory for PDFs,
# exports and other files. Relative paths resolve against the working directory.
# POLARIS_DATABASE_URL=sqlite+aiosqlite:///./polaris_dev.db
# POLARIS_DATA_DIR=./data

# ---- Models ----
# Polaris uses the Claude API with one fixed model. The key and endpoint come
# from the environment (there is no in-app form for them). The first pair below
# that has a key wins, and the endpoint comes from that same pair. With no base
# URL, requests go to api.anthropic.com. Base URLs work with or without a
# trailing /v1. Restart the engine after changing any of these.
#
# 1. Polaris-specific (POLARIS_CLAUDE_BASE_URL, when set, always wins)
# POLARIS_CLAUDE_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# POLARIS_CLAUDE_BASE_URL=http://your-gateway:4000
# 2. The standard Anthropic variables
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=http://your-gateway:4000
# 3. A LiteLLM gateway that serves Anthropic's native /v1/messages
# LITELLM_API_KEY=sk-...
# LITELLM_API_BASE=http://your-gateway:4000
#
# The model. Override only with another adaptive-thinking Claude model
# (Opus 5 / Sonnet 5 / Fable 5 family).
# POLARIS_CLAUDE_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# Embeddings and rerank come from the gateway's OpenAI-compatible endpoints
# ({base}/v1/embeddings, {base}/v1/rerank), so they need a gateway base URL.
# With a direct Anthropic key, search falls back to keywords.
# POLARIS_EMBEDDING_MODEL=BGE-M3
# POLARIS_RERANK_MODEL=BGE-Reranker-V2-M3
# Fall back to the built-in fake provider when there is no key
# (tests / key-less demos only, off by default).
# POLARIS_LLM_FAKE_FALLBACK=1
# The assistant's multi-turn tool loop is on by default; set 0 to turn it off.
# POLARIS_CHAT_AGENT_ENABLED=0

# ---- Literature APIs ----
# Semantic Scholar (optional; rate limits are tighter without a key)
# POLARIS_S2_API_KEY=
# Venue metrics use OpenAlex anonymously by default. EasyScholar is optional.
# POLARIS_EASYSCHOLAR_SECRET_KEYS=
# Outbound proxy for literature APIs, when arXiv/S2/OpenAlex are unreliable
# directly. Model and intranet traffic does not go through it.
# POLARIS_OUTBOUND_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:7897

# ---- MCP links ----
# Server root used only by stdio MCP download links. HTTP MCP always reuses
# the origin of the current /mcp request.
# POLARIS_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000
